title: Dealing with Toleration
new-page: true
is-card: true
card-image: img/portraits/BrüningHeinrich.jpg
view-if: dealing_with_toleration_timer = 0 and sdapo_toleration and chancellor_party == "CSP"
on-arrival: dealing_with_toleration_timer += 6; month_actions += 1
tags: govt_affairs
#subtitle: Despite not being in government, we can still provide support.

= Dealing with Toleration

We are currently acting as external support to the government of Chancellor [+ chancellor +]. How should we use our position?

- @break_toleration
- @urge_against_austerity
- @unity_sway
- @unity_enact_1
- @unity_enact_2
- @improve_relations
- @new_grand_coalition
- @stay_course: Stay the course, for stability's sake.
- @easy_discard

@break_toleration
view-if: not constructive_vonc
title: End the toleration agreement with a vote of no confidence!

Are we sure about this? A vote of no confidence would trigger new elections, and potentially an increased vote-share for the extremist parties.

- @vonc: Yes, end this arrangement!
- @stay_course: No, we should stay the course.

@vonc
on-arrival: sdapo_in_government = 0; sdapo_toleration = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; chancellor = "Seipel"; chancellor_party = "CSP"; next_election_time = time + 3 if next_election_time > time+3; next_election_month = month + 3 if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year = year if next_election_time >= time+3; next_election_year += 1 if next_election_month > 12; next_election_month -= 12 if next_election_month > 12; sdapo_toleration = 0; left_strength += 8; new_middle_sdapo -= 3; rural_sdapo -= 3; old_middle_sdapo -= 3; catholics_sdapo -= 3; reformist_dissent += 5; left_dissent -= 5

We have called for a vote of no confidence, and have brought down this government. Chancellor [+ chancellor +] currently rules as acting chancellor.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].

@urge_against_austerity
title: Urge the coalition against austerity politics, and to increase social spending.
choose-if: budget >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: This can only happen with a budget surplus.
go-to: urge_success if gdvp_relation >= 30 and csp_relation >= 40; urge_failure if gdvp_relation < 30 or csp_relation < 40

@urge_success
on-arrival: welfare += 1; budget -= 1; workers_sdapo += 4*(1-dissent); workers_csp += 1; unemployed_sdapo += 5*(1-dissent); csp_relation -= 3; gdvp_relation -= 3; reformist_dissent -= 5; center_dissent -= 5; labor_dissent -= 5;

We have successfully urged the coalition parties to increase social spending! Unfortunately, the center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations.

@urge_failure
on-arrival: csp_relation -= 3; gdvp_relation -= 3

Unfortunately, our negotiations have met with failure. The center-right parties increasingly see us as a nuisance, and might not wish to continue these negotiations.

@unity_sway
title: Urge the coalition to adopt the Unity Plan.
view-if: unity_plan_adopted != 1 and unity_rejected != 1 and moderate_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: unity_willingness == 1
unavailable-subtitle: The governing coalition is not willing to be convinced of the plan's merits.
go-to: unity_plan

@unity_enact_1
title: Urge the coalition to enact the Weimar Plan.
view-if: unity_plan_adopted == 1
choose-if: budget >= 2 and unemployed >= 8 and gdvp_relation >= 30 and csp_relation >= 40
unavailable-subtitle: There is not enough budget to enact the plan.
go-to: weimar_success if ((((((lb_relation/4)+csp_relation)+((dnsap_r*nazi_urgency)-(sdapo_r/2)-(csp_r)+unemployed)*(1-dissent))))-((100-gdvp_relation)*2)) >= 50; weimar_failure if ((((((lb_relation/4)+csp_relation)+((dnsap_r*nazi_urgency)-(sdapo_r/2)-(z_r)+unemployed)*(1-dissent))))-((100-gdvp_relation)*2)) < 50

@unity_success
on-arrival: budget -= 2; works_program += 1; unemployed -= 3 if unemployed >= 8; inflation += 1.5; workers_sdapo += 4*(1-dissent); workers_lb += 2; unemployed_sdapo += 3*(1-dissent); unemployed_lb += 1; new_middle_sdapo += 1*(1-dissent); new_middle_lb += 2; old_middle_csp += 1; old_middle_lb += 1; rural_sdapo += 1*(1-dissent); rural_csp += 1; moderate_plan_progress += 1; inflation += 1 if unemployed < 10; csp_relation -= 5; gdvp_relation -= 10; unity_dissent += 1

The coalition has, albeit reluctantly, agreed to enact the Weimar Plan under the CSP’s guidance! However, the coalition is increasingly viewing us as a nuisance and may cease implementation of the plan.

@unity_failure
on-arrival: workers_sdapo -= 2; unemployed_sdapo -= 3; left_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; reformist_dissent += 5; reformist_strength -= 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_strength -= 10; csp_relation -= 5; gdvp_relation -= 5; lb_relation -= 2; unity_dissent += 2

Despite the protests of our United allies in the coalition, our economic plan remains unenacted. This has discredited the Weimar Plan and has hurt our relations with the governing parties as well as our support.

@improve_relations
title: Improve relations with the parties of the coalition.
on-arrival: csp_relation += 5*(1-dissent); gdvp_relation += 4*(1-dissent); left_dissent += 5;

We have increased our level of contact and discussions with the parties of the coalition, primarily the CSP and GDVP.

Our attempts to reach out to the center-right are met with disdain by leftists within our party.




@new_grand_coalition
title: Can we join the government in a new grand coalition?
choose-if: csp_relation >= 50 and gdvp_relation >= 30 and resources >= 2
subtitle: We will need 2 resources to smooth out the process of forming the coalition.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if csp_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the CSP. ?][? if gdvp_relation < 30 : We do not have adequate relations with the GDVP. ?] [? if resources < 2 : We do not have enough resources. ?]
on-arrival: resources -= 2; sdapo_in_government = 1; in_grand_coalition = 1; sdapo_toleration = 0; left_dissent += 6; reformist_strength += 5; leverage = 20 if leverage >= 20
achievement: constitutional_coalition

Our negotiations have succeeded, and the CSP and GDVP have agreed to form a new coalition government with us!

We are now part of a "constitutional coalition" government that includes all parties except the extremists of the KPO, Heimwehr and DNSAP. [+ chancellor +] will remain as chancellor. Leftists in our party are skeptical of this arrangement.

- @election_1928.ministries: Now, we must select our ministries.



@stay_course

We will stay the course of toleration, for the sake of stability.
